  "details": "Version: 2021.3.2\nSummary: Upgraded unity project to 2019.4.29 and went to upload my avatar. Upon doing so I got the error message \"uh oh, something went wrong\" and it recommended me to remove the blueprint id. I removed the blueprint id and still got the error message. I went further and removed the blueprint id and avatar descriptor and even freshly reinstalled the sdk and still got the same message.\nNote: When I log into the SDK, it will show that i'm logged in and that I have access to my content, but on the error screen it says that I don't own it. It will also log me out the sdk after exiting the upload screen which has never happened to me before.",
